# PTCG AI Battle Challenge — Strategy Research

This project is competition-research code developed for the **Pokémon TCG AI
Battle Challenge** (Kaggle Simulation + Strategy tracks).

**Ownership notice.** This repository contains original research code authored
for this challenge. It also wraps the official **CABT** Python engine
(`kaggle-environments` → `kaggle_environments.envs.cabt`), which is a
third-party competition component distributed under its own terms and **is not**
part of the original contribution here.

**No license grants redistribution of the competition engine or dataset.** The
CABT engine (`cg.dll` and its bindings) and the competition card dataset are
third-party / competition assets. Unless their own license expressly permits
redistribution, these components **must not be mirrored** in this repository.
See [`docs/DATASET.md`](docs/DATASET.md) for what must be downloaded from
Kaggle and where the repository expects it, and
[`docs/ENGINE_LIMITATION.md`](docs/ENGINE_LIMITATION.md) for the engine
capability audit.

**Limitation of use.** This code is made available so that the competition
strategy, evidence, and reproducibility methodology can be inspected. The
author grants no license to use this code to re-enter or re-derive a
competition submission on their behalf, and makes no warranty of any kind.

Third-party component attributions:

- `kaggle_environments` (CABT engine bindings): Copyright (c) their respective
  authors; distributed under its own license. Bundled engine binaries are
  competition assets, not part of the original work here.
- Card dataset: provided under the competition's dataset terms. The CSVs/PDF
  expected by this repository are **not redistributed**; see
  `docs/DATASET.md` for acquisition instructions.
